  "tolerances": {
    "_rationale": "The oracle is an external cross-check of observable behaviour, not a second implementation of the runner contract. It evaluates no gates, produces no capability report, and emits no receipts, so those three surfaces are declared tolerable here and nowhere else: they are structurally absent, not behaviourally different. Step identity, method, per-step status and the terminal code are compared strictly — those are what the two lanes must agree on.",
